{
  "_comment": [
    "Tailscale provider for the VPN bar widget.",
    "",
    "Drop the .sample suffix (or run `nirimaki tailscale install`,",
    "which auto-activates this file) and Tailscale will show up in",
    "the VPN bar pill's popover.",
    "",
    "Requires `tailscale` in PATH (package: tailscale). connectCmd /",
    "disconnectCmd both call the plain CLI, which only works when",
    "the daemon is set to grant your user unprivileged control:",
    "",
    "    sudo tailscale set --operator=$USER",
    "",
    "Otherwise `tailscale up/down` will demand sudo and the popover",
    "buttons will silently fail. `nirimaki tailscale install` runs",
    "the operator command for you; on existing installs run it once",
    "manually.",
    "",
    "Initial sign-in still happens via `sudo tailscale up` from a",
    "terminal — the connect button doesn't drive the device-auth",
    "URL flow.",
    "",
    "statusLabelCmd extracts the connected hostname so the bar pill",
    "tooltip reads 'Tailscale · my-laptop' instead of just",
    "'Tailscale'."
  ],
  "id":               "tailscale",
  "name":             "Tailscale",
  "icon":             "󰦝",
  "statusCmd":        ["sh", "-lc", "tailscale status --json | jq -r .BackendState"],
  "statusOnPattern":  "^Running$",
  "statusLabelCmd":   ["sh", "-lc", "tailscale status --json | jq -r '.Self.DNSName // .Self.HostName | rtrimstr(\".\")'"],
  "connectCmd":       ["tailscale", "up"],
  "disconnectCmd":    ["tailscale", "down"],
  "pollSeconds":      5
}
